WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:01.868
A house divided

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.602
over military

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.070
and financial aid to Ukraine.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.238
So brand new CNN reporting

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.906
reveals a growing chasm

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.041
among the GOP

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.876
as the war enters its second year

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.111
Some hard line Republicans

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:13.213
say the billions spent back in Ukraine

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.081
is a prime example of government waste.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.183
And given their slim House majority,

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.651
it could be enough to complicate

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.953
or potentially

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:20.820
even block

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.288
additional funding down the road.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.723
Joining us now to share their reporting

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.525
and their insights, CNN's M.J.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.826
Lee, CNN's Isaac

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.028
over to Mitchell

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.562
of the Atlanta Journal-Constitution.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.431
And CNN's Lauren Fox.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:33.400
So the House Republicans, you report

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.334
it's a minority,

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.002
but it's a vocal minority

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.204
who say America first.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.472
What are we doing

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.607
Where's the money going?

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.808
Yeah, and it's been a dramatic

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.143
split screen this week.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.011
While you've had the president

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.046
visiting Ukraine,

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.747
you have had a lot of these House

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:48.748
Republicans arguing

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.216
he shouldn't be there in the first place.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.052
He should be back in the United States.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.754
So I think one of the biggest chasms

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.489
that you're starting to see right now

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.058
is just fatigue about

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:01.227
why is the US spending money at all.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:02.762
And it's a real big difference

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.197
between the leadership

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.765
and some of these rank and file members.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.200
You have people like Mitch McConnell

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.868
who are going to go out there and argue

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:09.235
all day

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.170
long on Fox News

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.571
that this is an important issue

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.239
for the Republican base.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.975
Then you have people like Kevin McCarthy,

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:16.643
who's going to have to

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.344
contend with some of those conservatives

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.380
like Matt Gates, who has a resolution

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.282
asserting American fatigue

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.616
over giving Ukraine

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.919
financial aid for this war.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:26.553
Kevin McCarthy

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.621
said he did not support that resolution.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.256
But he also doesn't support

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.124
a blank check.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.826
And that leads to a lot of question marks

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.194
as this fight on Capitol Hill

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.195
really intensifies

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.796
over spending over the next

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.331
several months.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.365
What does that mean

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.533
for the future of Ukraine?

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.836
And this isolationist movement

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:43.903
is growing in the republic

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.972
where it's not new, but it is growing.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.340
And you see, it's in

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:47.907
your noteworthy

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:48.875
many House Republicans said,

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.243
what is President Biden doing there?

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:50.810
The last few days,

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.345
they did not seem to question.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.680
While their own House Foreign Affairs

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.214
Committee Chairman,

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:54.881
Mike McFaul

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:55.849
was there, leading

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.450
a bipartisan delegation of House members,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.418
he was in Kyiv right after

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:58.952
President Biden.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.420
I didn't see any tweets saying

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.621
why isn't he back in Texas?

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:02.522
Why isn't he at the border?

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.257
They seem to have forgotten that part.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:04.991
It's interesting, though,

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.025
because over in the Senate,

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.627
most Republicans in the Senate

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.461
think this is a fight

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.496
the United States must be

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:10.897
and most Republicans in the Senate.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:11.831
This is an area where they say

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.399
President Biden is doing the right thing.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.434
They might even want him to do more.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.735
Shelley Moore, Capitol,

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:16.803
Republican of West Virginia.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.403
Maybe they aren't

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:18.705
getting the same information,

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:19.772
she says of House members.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:20.640
I think maybe

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.708
there are more people over there

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.510
who view it as an enhancement of war,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.612
where we see it as protection of freedom.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.280
That's what President Biden

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.214
has been saying,

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.049
that if you give Putin Ukraine,

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:30.850
what's to stop him

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.086
from going into Estonia, Latvia, Moldova,

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.320
those group of nine countries

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.221
we just showed?

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:35.488
Yeah.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.290
And I think what

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.258
the more seasoned

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:39.759
Republicans, the Republicans

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:40.326
who've been around,

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.828
we have to remember the House,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:42.495
especially this

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.898
new kind of more empowered, far right

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.033
contingent of the House

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.569
has not been around a really long time.

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:52.338
But those senators who had say,

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:55.141
if you empower Putin and quite frankly,

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.010
even this rhetoric around

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.279
withdrawing US funding

00:02:59.279 --> 00:02:59.946
is something

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.381
that can further empower

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.483
Putin to say, hey, I can stay the race

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.452
and hope to wait out the US

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.254
and then bide my time.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.122
And I think

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.690
what we're hearing from senators

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.126
is that you can't let that happen.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:13.760
The question

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.061
is, will the House

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.129
that new Republican

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:16.930
majority start

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.232
standing in the way of further U.S.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.333
support for the Ukraine?

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.334
And what makes it all

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.402
the more interesting is

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:22.802
as we head

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.170
into the presidential cycle, it's

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.672
not just a House Republican

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.173
or even an internal House

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.107
Republican divide.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:28.508
You see it

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.143
playing out on the campaign trail

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.211
among declared

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.979
and likely soon to be Republican

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:33.813
presidential candidates

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:38.117
the war in Ukraine.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:41.287
It's more than just about Ukraine.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:43.489
This is a war about freedom

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.190
and it's a war

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.258
we have to win

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:46.459
They have effectively

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.228
a blank check policy

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.862
with no clear strategic

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.598
objective identified.

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:54.534
And these things can can escalate.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.236
And I don't think it's in our interest

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:56.970
to be getting

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.672
into a proxy war with China.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.307
Is this a fight?

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:01.975
President Biden

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:03.810
wants to have on the campaign trail,

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.011
or is there any concern

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:05.612
at the White House

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:06.713
that if this is a either

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.214
or campaign issue, it undermines

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.115
the effort in Congress?

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:09.482
Well, look,

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.416
I would say that

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.552
I think the last 72 hours have shown

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:13.720
what a tough hand

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.722
Republicans have to play in many ways.

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:16.222
Right.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.390
We've had this president,

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.426
who has made a dangerous trip into a war

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.028
zone, has been sticking his finger

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.696
in the eye of Vladimir Putin

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:24.297
and standing

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.865
next to an international hero.

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.900
That being Volodymyr Zelensky,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.801
American voters

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.003
like seeing a president

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.070
who looks strong on

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.106
the international world stage,

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.974
particularly heading into a war zone.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.243
On such an unprecedented trip.

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.344
And Republicans

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.480
want to sort of make something political

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.781
out of something

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:42.782
that is very challenging

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:43.950
for them to deal with.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.752
The imagery of the president

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.786
making this trip has been

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:47.620
something challenging

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.255
for Republicans to deal with.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:50.957
But I think, you know, Lauren,

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.759
you make a really good point about how

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:53.192
this isn't

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.861
really the majority of Republicans

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:56.996
in the Republican Party.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:57.797
In large part,

00:04:57.797 --> 00:04:59.532
they are supportive of continuing

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:01.934
to fight against Vladimir Putin.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.936
But I think someone like Kevin McCarthy,

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:05.605
he hasn't really made clear

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.306
what exactly

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:07.206
he means when he says

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.941
there's not going to be a blank check

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.076
made out to Ukraine.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:10.877
Pick your cycle.

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:12.278
Presidential primaries often

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.713
settle debates in parties.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.080
Bill Clinton

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.214
was the different kind of Democrat.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.149
George W Bush wanted

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.383
compassionate conservatism.

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.651
Donald Trump rewrote

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.186
the rules of Republican politics.

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.721
Will this debate be settled?

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.322
Well, look,

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.190
what we're going to is already

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.291
Nikki Haley is saying that

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:27.727
if we don't continue in the war with

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.028
and for Ukraine,

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.396
then that will lead to World War Three.

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.230
Donald Trump is saying

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.498
if we do continue it,

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:33.800
that will lead to World War Three.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.034
That's where the Republican Party

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:35.968
is divided on this.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.236
And then you get into all the House

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:37.770
dynamics.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.239
All this is going to be something

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.175
where you have a lot of Republicans

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.443
who are facing

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.444
this isolation is

00:05:44.444 --> 00:05:46.612
the idea is also budget ideas,

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:47.580
but trying to figure out

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.048
how they attack Joe Biden

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.950
and how they make Biden the bad guy here.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:51.918
As MJ said,

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:54.220
he through the imagery of this week,

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.488
made that a little bit tricky for them.

